https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KZBVAGBYPos  (Capo 0)

With all due respect to the red-headed stranger, Bob Wills is the master of western swing and it's his version that's presented here.

TIP:  The intro is a two-beat walk-down beginning with the open 3rd string <g>.  Then it's 4th string/3rd fret, 2nd fret, 1st fret, open 4th fret; 5th string/3rd fret, 2nd fret, open 5th string and (G) etc.  (Notes may or may not transpose.) 

TIP:  The nature of swing music is the verses are just about one big run-on sentence so you just go with it.

TIP:  The first part of the longer instrumental bridge is a bit tricky to keep up with as it's a faster pace.  Just keep it moving along with two-counts on each chord until you get back to the fiddle part. 
 
    
